{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-14_22-44-04-hashicorp_raft-real-run/draft && python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nd={\\\"rationale\\\":\\\"Registered the one consequence of the no-snapshot variant that is still derived from source rather than observed, so it is recorded as necessary work rather than left implicit. A node whose configuration is empty skips the membership check in requestVote, so it would grant a vote to any candidate that passes the log up-to-dateness test, including a candidate that appears in no configuration the node holds; the observation that it refuses to campaign rests on the election gate and is now executed, but the vote side was not exercised. The gap names the discriminator that would settle it and the parent and child accounts are otherwise unchanged.\\\",\n \\\"gaps\\\":[\n  {\\\"investigation_id\\\":\\\"16929a65990d446dad09fb1f6c9fe1a2-question-0\\\",\n   \\\"question\\\":\\\"Does a node running with an empty configuration actually grant its vote to a candidate that appears in no configuration it holds, and can such a grant let a candidate that the current cluster would not admit be elected?\\\"}],\n \\\"interpretations\\\":[\n  {\\\"investigation_id\\\":\\\"16929a65990d446dad09fb1f6c9fe1a2-question-0\\\",\n   \\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"s-votegrant\\\",\\\"s-election-gate\\\",\\\"s-quorumsize\\\",\\\"s-scan\\\"],\n   \\\"executions\\\":{\\\"d2973ec8cc524a9089c63dd046e1a4ff\\\":[2,4,0],\\\"bdf2837a4c004f95b6c9b19db4fb8154\\\":[1,2,0]},\n   \\\"joint_history\\\":\\\"Two receipts of two fixed experiments on this question: bdf2837a4c004f95b6c9b19db4fb8154 records the restarts and the configuration each produces (empty with the feature, {A,B,C} without it), and d2973ec8cc524a9089c63dd046e1a4ff is the revision of the same harness that adds the isolation phase and records campaigning. Both observe the same cluster identity, the same restart procedure and the same two resulting configurations, and each comparison outcome is read from its own receipt.\\\",\n   \\\"conclusion\\\":\\\"explained\\\",\\\"defect_claim\\\":\\\"asserted\\\",\n   \\\"rationale\\\":\\\"Answer: a node restarted with Config.RestoreCommittedLogs while it has no snapshot comes up with an empty configuration and, when isolated, never campaigns; a control restart of the same stores without the feature rebuilds {A,B,C} and does campaign. Receipts bdf2837a4c004f95b6c9b19db4fb8154 (configurations after each restart) and d2973ec8cc524a9089c63dd046e1a4ff (isolated campaigning) establish that, with the mechanism being the scan start max(lastSnapshotIndex, lastApplied)+1 combined with the replay that raises lastApplied to the persisted commit index, plus the election gate that refuses to campaign while latestIndex is zero (raft.go 225-246). One consequence remains unobserved and is registered as a necessary gap: an empty configuration also skips the membership check in requestVote (raft.go 1660-1680), so the node would grant a vote to a candidate it cannot see; the discriminator is to let a real candidate campaign while such a node is reachable and observe whether the vote is granted and, for a node the current configuration would not admit, whether that grant contributes to a leadership the cluster would not otherwise produce. Limits otherwise unchanged: construction-state observation with a 300ms settle, harness-arranged absence of snapshots rather than a store failure, a one-second transport-only isolation with no vote solicitation, in-memory stores with scaled timeouts.\\\",\n   \\\"answers\\\":{\\\"@missing\\\": None}}]}\n# strip the placeholder answers entry: gaps are registered without answers here\nd['interpretations'][0].pop('answers')\njson.dump(d,open('update.json','w'),indent=2,ensure_ascii=False)\nprint('written')\nPY\ncd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-14_22-44-04-hashicorp_raft-real-run && /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python -I -B -c \\\"import sys; sys.path.insert(0, '/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src'); from consensus_assurance.cli import main; raise SystemExit(main())\\\" validate --run /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-14_22-44-04-hashicorp_raft-real-run --submission update.json 2>&1 | tail -3\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
