{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_19","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-14_22-44-04-hashicorp_raft-real-run/submissions/e5bb935fcbd847dea7ecc816ef54ae88 && ls && python3 -c \\\"\nimport json\na=json.load(open('accepted.json'))\nprint(json.dumps(a,indent=1)[:4000])\n\\\"\"","aggregated_output":"accepted.json\ninputs\nraw.json\n{\n \"rationale\": \"Interpreted the isolation receipt and closed the containment question. Receipt d2973ec8cc524a9089c63dd046e1a4ff evaluated all four comparisons as declared: the feature-enabled node, whose configuration is empty, was isolated for a second and never campaigned (configured_servers 0, campaigning_observed false), while the control holding {A,B,C} became a candidate (configured_servers 3, campaigning_observed true). Both kept their term, which the operands show; that is the pre-vote extension rather than a failure to campaign, so the term stays an operand. The child account was rewritten so the refusal to campaign is an executed observation rather than a source-derived one, leaving only the vote-granting behaviour with an empty configuration as source-derived.\",\n \"sources\": [],\n \"investigations\": [],\n \"knowledge\": [],\n \"gaps\": [],\n \"interpretations\": [\n  {\n   \"investigation_id\": \"16929a65990d446dad09fb1f6c9fe1a2-question-0\",\n   \"experiment_id\": \"b13748bdaa85486486b1324eb1032ff3-experiment\",\n   \"source_ids\": [\n    \"s-election-gate\",\n    \"s-votegrant\",\n    \"s-quorumsize\",\n    \"s-scan\"\n   ],\n   \"executions\": {\n    \"d2973ec8cc524a9089c63dd046e1a4ff\": [\n     2,\n     4,\n     0\n    ]\n   },\n   \"conclusion\": \"holds\",\n   \"defect_claim\": null,\n   \"rationale\": \"This experiment characterises containment rather than a defect, and its predicates are all satisfied. Admission index 0 records the fixture (no snapshots on A, ten committed commands, A reporting {A,B,C} while running). After the feature-enabled restart, isolating the node from every peer for one second - twenty heartbeat timeouts at the configured 50ms - left it a follower that never entered candidate or leader state, with zero configured servers (comparisons 0 and 1 hold at index 2). The control restart, holding three configured servers, became a candidate during the same isolation (comparisons 2 and 3 hold at index 4), so the isolation is a real trigger and the empty configuration is what keeps the feature-enabled node from campaigning. Both nodes kept their term across the window (3 to 3, operands at indices 2 and 4), which the pre-vote extension explains: a candidate runs a pre-vote before incrementing its term, so the control could be observed in candidate state without a term change. Limits: the observation is a 1-second sample every 5ms in one run per mode, no votes were solicited from real peers, and the fault injected is transport disconnection only.\",\n   \"answers\": {},\n   \"knowledge\": [],\n   \"counterevidence\": [\n    \"The control's candidate state shows the isolation would produce campaigning if a configuration were present, so the feature-enabled node's silence is attributable to the empty configuration.\",\n    \"The unchanged terms in both modes show the term operand must not be read as evidence of campaigning either way, given pre-vote.\"\n   ],\n   \"limitations\": [\n    \"One second of sampling per mode, no repetition across schedules.\",\n    \"No votes are solicited, so no election outcome is executed for either mode.\",\n    \"Transport disconnection is the only fault; no crash or store failure is involved.\"\n   ],\n   \"joint_history\": \"\",\n   \"failure_attribution\": null\n  },\n  {\n   \"investigation_id\": \"16929a65990d446dad09fb1f6c9fe1a2-question-0\",\n   \"experiment_id\": null,\n   \"source_ids\": [\n    \"s-scan\",\n    \"s-restorecommitted\",\n    \"s-processlogs\",\n    \"s-confentry\",\n    \"s-quorumsize\",\n    \"s-election-gate\",\n    \"s-votegrant\"\n   ],\n   \"executions\": {\n    \"d2973ec8cc524a9089c63dd046e1a4ff\": [\n     2,\n     4,\n     0\n    ],\n    \"bdf2837a4c004f95b6c9b19db4fb8154\": [\n     1,\n     2,\n     0\n    ]\n   },\n   \"conclusion\": \"explained\",\n   \"defect_claim\": \"asserted\",\n   \"rationale\": \"Answer: a node restarted with Config.RestoreCommittedLogs while it has no snapshot comes up with an empty configuration, and the election gate keeps that from turning into a stray candidate. Receipt bdf2837a4c004f95b6c9b19db4fb8154 records the restarts: the feature-enabled node reports no server\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
