{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_20","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-14_22-44-04-hashicorp_raft-real-run && python3 -c \\\"\nimport json\nd=json.load(open('research.json'))\nfor iv in d['investigations']:\n    print(json.dumps(iv)[:900]); print('===')\n\\\"\"","aggregated_output":"{\"id\": \"e99a162d27c7421fa6729d8cb9703581-question-0\", \"version\": 2, \"question\": \"When Config.RestoreCommittedLogs replays committed logs during NewRaft, which configuration does the restarted node end up using for candidate admission and election quorum if its last snapshot predates a committed configuration entry that its own log already contains?\", \"hypothesis\": \"The eager replay moves lastApplied to the persisted commit index before the configuration scan, so the scan starts above the committed configuration entry; r.configurations.latest and r.configurations.committed remain the snapshot's configuration, and the node derives quorumSize/hasVote from that older membership until some later configuration entry is appended.\", \"discriminator\": \"Same restart-shaped stores (snapshot index 5 with configuration {A,B,C}, log index 6 = committed LogConfiguration{A,B,C,D,E}, persisted commit inde\n===\n{\"id\": \"e99a162d27c7421fa6729d8cb9703581-question-1\", \"version\": 2, \"question\": \"Can NewRaft fail to return when Config.RestoreCommittedLogs replays more committed log entries than processLogs can enqueue on fsmMutateCh before runFSM is started?\", \"hypothesis\": \"restoreFromCommittedLogs runs before goFunc(r.runFSM); processLogs blocks once fsmMutateCh (buffered 128) is full, and each batch holds up to MaxAppendEntries entries, so a replay of more than 128*MaxAppendEntries committed entries leaves the constructor waiting for a consumer that does not exist yet.\", \"discriminator\": \"Construct a node whose CommitTrackingLogStore reports a commit index at least 128*MaxAppendEntries+1 entries above the snapshot/applied index and observe whether NewRaft returns, with the batch-consumer set (runFSM started or not) as the changing condition.\", \"disposition\": \"explained\", \"parent_id\": null, \"source\n===\n{\"id\": \"3eae8e12b0574799b781f10f7899dbad-question-0\", \"version\": 2, \"question\": \"Can a node whose configuration was left stale by the RestoreCommittedLogs replay actually win an election with fewer votes than a majority of the configuration recorded in its own committed log, while the remaining voters elect their own leader?\", \"hypothesis\": \"With the restarted node holding {A,B,C} while its log records the committed {A,B,C,D,E}, isolating it with one voter of the stale set lets it collect two votes (itself plus that voter) against its stale quorum of two and become leader, while the three remaining voters, who hold the current configuration, elect a second leader; both then accept commands.\", \"discriminator\": \"One cluster whose only difference is the defect: node A is restarted with RestoreCommittedLogs after a committed configuration change beyond its snapshot, then a partition separate\n===\n{\"id\": \"12a64c3fb3bc403f9a55aa626c4f81eb-question-0\", \"version\": 2, \"question\": \"Which permitted mechanism reconciles the divergent entries and applied state left by the stale-configuration split: does the library engage installSnapshot, log compaction or a user restore on its own once the cluster is whole, or does the divergence persist while the node participates normally?\", \"hypothesis\": \"Nothing in the ordinary AppendEntries path reconciles same-term conflicts, and the stale node keeps serving and replicating, so it never falls far enough behind for the leader to send a snapshot; only an explicit snapshot install (forced by compaction plus a lagging follower), a user Restore or a truncation caused by a different term would replace the divergent entry and FSM state.\", \"discriminator\": \"After the healed split state, force the surviving leader to snapshot and compact past the follower's\n===\n{\"id\": \"16929a65990d446dad09fb1f6c9fe1a2-question-0\", \"version\": 2, \"question\": \"Which configuration does a node end up with when it is restarted with Config.RestoreCommittedLogs while it has no snapshot at all, so the log scan is the only mechanism that could rebuild its membership?\", \"hypothesis\": \"Because the scan starts at max(lastSnapshotIndex, lastApplied)+1 and the replay raises lastApplied to the persisted commit index, a node with no snapshot processes no configuration entry at all and comes up with an empty configuration, whereas the same restart without the feature scans from index 1 and rebuilds the membership.\", \"discriminator\": \"The same stores restarted with and without the feature: the feature-enabled restart is predicted to report an empty configuration while the control reports the bootstrap membership.\", \"disposition\": \"explained\", \"parent_id\": \"e99a162d27c7421fa6729d8\n===\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
